@user-51 Good catch — thank you! You're right that dropping `source_image` outright leaves downstream consumers (RF-DETR's visualize path and anything else following that convention) without a parent image reference.

I've adopted your restoration pattern into #2599 (79cd123): after the merge, a dropped `source_image` key is restored to the full input image when the slicer input is an `np.ndarray`, and the drop warning now mentions the restoration when it applies. It's covered by tests for both directions — including the case where the *first* slice lacks the key — plus regression tests for a related union bug the Copilot review caught (keys carried only by later slices weren't being dropped, so that path still crashed).

Full credit to you for the restoration semantics in the changelog/PR notes. Happy to consolidate on whichever PR the maintainers prefer — #2599 or your #2596 — just say the word and I'll help land either.
